      "updated": 1757400000000,
      "version": 1,
      "seed": 1256858368,
      "versionNonce": 1052731334,
      "boundElements": null,
      "id": "n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 1299.5,
      "height": 80.0,
      "text": "Note: the Intake API only puts the event on the queue and returns 202 right away — it does not wait for the send result.\n② guards the intake stage and ⑤ guards the worker stage (ADR 0003). If the UPDATE at ⑤ changes 0 rows,\nanother worker already took the message, so this one moves on quietly.\nIf the worker dies after ⑥ but before the result is recorded, a duplicate can still go out — so the provider gets the same key too.",
      "originalText": "Note: the Intake API only puts the event on the queue and returns 202 right away — it does not wait for the send result.\n② guards the intake stage and ⑤ guards the worker stage (ADR 0003). If the UPDATE at ⑤ changes 0 rows,\nanother worker already took the message, so this one moves on quietly.\nIf the worker dies after ⑥ but before the result is recorded, a duplicate can still go out — so the provider gets the same key too.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
